ALE Seminar Series\nParticipating Seminars\nParticipating Algebraic Topology Seminar\nParticipating Analysis Seminar\nParticipating Computer-Assisted Proofs Seminar\nParticipating Funct. Analysis Seminar\nParticipating Number Theory Seminar\nParticipating PDE Seminar\nParticipating Probability Seminar\nParticipating Topology Seminar\nWeekly Events Schedule\nAlumni\nGiving\nContact\nSearch\nMenu\nMenu\nFinancial Support\nFinancial Support\nIn recent years, we have been able to guarantee 5 years of full financial support to almost all students admitted to the Ph.D. program. Guaranteed support provides income that is enough for living expenses (exact amounts vary from year to year), and in addition provides full registration fees, health insurance, and, for students who are not residents of California, non-resident tuition. (US students are expected to establish California residency after their first year.) Financial support typically consists of a combination of teaching assistantships (TA), research assistantships (RA), and fellowships, including, in some cases, fellowships supported by NSF Research and Training Grants (RTG fellowships). Applicants are automatically considered for these kinds of support; no separate application is needed. Applicants are encouraged to separately apply for extramural fellowships, such as the National Science Foundation Graduate Research Fellowships and the Hertz and Ford Fellowships.\nReaderships\nThe Department employs a number of students (both graduate and undergraduate) as readers to grade homework papers. All readers must have at least a 3.2 GPA and must have taken at least two years of college calculus. Applications are accepted at various times throughout the year.\nNeed-Based Financial Aid & Loans\nThe UCLA Financial Aid Office allocates funds to graduate students based on financial need. Such awards include long-term, low interest loans. Foreign students are not eligible. Interested students should contact the Financial Aid Office directly.\nExtramural Support\nStudents interested in extramural fellowships should review the Graduate Division publication, Graduate and Postdoctoral Extramural Support or browse the GRAPES Database. Students can also contact the Special Fellowships Office. Students are encouraged to apply for the NSF Graduate Research Fellowship.\nPages\n2023 MSRI Satellite Workshop Registration\n2026-2027 Dissertation Year Award Application\nAdmissions\nAdmissions\nAlgebra Research Page\nAll\nAlumni\nAlumni Update Form\nAnalysis Research Page\nAP Credit & Enrollment Information\nCAM Reports 1986-2000\nCAM Reports 2001-2020\nCAM Reports 2021-Current\nCareers in Mathematics Event Page\nCombinatorics Research Page\nComputational Applied Mathematics (CAM) Research Page\nContact\nCurtis Center\nDepartment Awards\nDepartment Overview\nDept. Magazine\nDissertation Year Award\nDistinguished Lecture Series\nDiversity & Inclusion\nElementor #8481\nEnrollment into Math and Programming In Computing (PIC) Courses\nFaculty\nFaculty Honors & Awards\nFaculty Positions 2026-27\nFall 2025 New Student Information\nFAQ\nFeedback\nFinancial Support\nFormatting Your UCLA Thesis\nFormer Faculty Honors and Awards\nFunctional Analysis Research Page\nGeometry Research Page\nGet Ready To Take The Diagnostic Test\nGiving\nGraduate Courses\nGraduate Handbook\nGraduate Program Overview\nGraduate School for Undergraduates\nGraduate Student Spotlight: Alexander Sietsema\nGraduate Student Spotlight: Arian Nadjimzadah\nGraduate Student Spotlight: Ariana Chin\nGraduate Student Spotlight: Yunuo Chen\nGraduate Student Travel Stipends\nGraduate Students\nHome\nInclusive Excellence Events\nKnowledge Base\nMajors, Minors & Specializations\nMath Course Request\nMath Department Policy on Grading Coordination\nMath Diagnostic Test\nMathematical and Statistical Finance (MSF) Research Page\nMathematical Logic Research Page\nMathematics Reading Room\nMerchandise Order Form\nNews & Events\nNews Archive\nNonlinear Phenom